{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And YHWH would speak to Moses face to face.</b> And He would converse with Moses." "<b>And he would return to the camp.</b> After He had spoken with him, Moses would return to the camp and teach the elders what he had learned. And this practice Moses maintained from Yom Kippur until the Mishkan was erected — and no longer. For on the seventeenth of Tammuz the tablets were broken, and on the eighteenth he burned the calf and judged the sinners, and on the nineteenth he went up, as it says ״וַיְהִי מִמָּחֳרָת וַיֹּאמֶר מֹשֶׁה אֶל הָעָם״ etc. (Exodus 32), and he spent forty days there and sought mercy, as it says ״וָאֶתְנַפַּל לִפְנֵי ה׳״ etc. (Deuteronomy 9), and on Rosh Chodesh Elul it was said to him ״וְעָלִיתָ בַבֹּקֶר אֶל הַר סִינַי״ (Exodus 34), to receive the latter tablets — and he spent forty days there, as is said of them ״וְאָנֹכִי עָמַדְתִּי בָהָר כַּיָּמִים הָרִאשׁוֹנִים״ etc. — just as the first ones were with favor, so the latter ones were with favor; deduce from this that the middle ones were in anger. On the tenth of Tishrei the Holy One, blessed be He, was reconciled to Israel with joy and a whole heart, and said to Moses ״I have forgiven,״ and handed him the latter tablets, and he came down and began to command them concerning the work of the Mishkan, and they made it until the first of Nisan, and from the time it was erected He no longer spoke with him except from the Tent of Meeting (Tanchuma)." "<b>And he would return to the camp.</b> Its Targum: וְתָיֵב לְמַשְׁרִיתָא — because it is in the present tense, and so the entire passage: <b>and all the people would see</b> — וְחָזַן; <b>and they would stand</b> — וְקָיְמִין; <b>and they would gaze</b> — וּמִסְתַּכְּלִין; <b>and they would bow down</b> — וְסָגְדִין. And its midrash: <b>And YHWH would speak to Moses</b> — that he should return to the camp — He said to him: I am angry and you are angry; if so, who will draw them near? (Tanchuma)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:27.454663552Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}